/**
 * Labels Go decodes with a stateful or multi-byte codec.
 *
 * The twin THROWS for these rather than producing bytes Go would not produce.
 * A loud, deterministic failure is the only honest option: silently passing the
 * bytes through would turn a UTF-16 body into U+FFFD soup that still "parses",
 * and guessing with TextDecoder would disagree with Go on the undefined
 * positions. The corpus contains none of them.
 */
